WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.968
It was the morning of Christmas Eve.

2
00:00:03.969 --> 00:00:06.964
Nello woke up and shivered.

3
00:00:06.965 --> 00:00:10.466
It was freezing inside the little hut.

4
00:00:10.467 --> 00:00:18.330
Nello held onto his closest friend, and his tears dropped onto the great dog's forehead.

5
00:00:18.331 --> 00:00:22.282
"Let's go, Patrasche," Nello murmured.

6
00:00:22.283 --> 00:00:25.535
"We won't wait to be kicked out."

7
00:00:25.536 --> 00:00:28.948
They stepped outside into the cold.

8
00:00:28.949 --> 00:00:34.088
Patrasche hung his head as he passed the little green cart.

9
00:00:34.089 --> 00:00:37.284
It didn't belong to him anymore.

10
00:00:37.285 --> 00:00:41.937
The farmer who owned the hut was taking it for the rent.

11
00:00:41.938 --> 00:00:46.611
He was taking everything else in the hut too.

12
00:00:46.612 --> 00:00:51.427
Nello and Patrasche walked the long road into Antwerp.

13
00:00:51.428 --> 00:00:56.551
It was the same road they had walked to deliver milk every day.

14
00:00:56.552 --> 00:00:59.475
It was still early morning.

15
00:00:59.476 --> 00:01:04.756
The windows were closed on most of the houses along the road.

16
00:01:04.757 --> 00:01:08.697
In a few houses, people were awake.

17
00:01:08.698 --> 00:01:12.858
At one house, the door stood open a little.

18
00:01:12.859 --> 00:01:17.186
Inside, an old woman was cooking breakfast.

19
00:01:17.187 --> 00:01:22.556
Nello's grandfather, Jehan, had been kind to her many times.

20
00:01:22.557 --> 00:01:29.614
"Do you have any leftovers for Patrasche?" Nello called timidly from the door.

21
00:01:29.615 --> 00:01:34.697
"He's old, and he's eaten nothing since yesterday."

22
00:01:34.698 --> 00:01:41.036
The old woman shut the door quickly, murmuring about the high price of flour.

23
00:01:41.037 --> 00:01:44.600
Nello and Patrasche kept walking.

24
00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:49.411
They didn't stop at any more houses.

25
00:01:49.412 --> 00:01:54.089
It was ten o'clock in the morning when they reached Antwerp.

26
00:01:54.090 --> 00:02:01.612
"I wish I had something I could sell, so I could buy some bread for Patrasche," thought Nello.

27
00:02:01.613 --> 00:02:08.139
But Nello had nothing, except the clothes he wore and his wooden shoes.

28
00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:11.249
Somehow Patrasche understood.

29
00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:16.018
He knew that Nello longed to ease his hunger and aches.

30
00:02:16.019 --> 00:02:19.500
He put his nose into Nello's hand.

31
00:02:19.501 --> 00:02:24.644
"Please, don't worry about me," he seemed to say.

32
00:02:24.645 --> 00:02:29.959
The winner of the art competition was to be announced at noon.

33
00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:35.903
Nello and Patrasche walked toward the public building in the middle of town.

34
00:02:35.904 --> 00:02:42.580
There, many young people crowded the steps and waited in the street.

35
00:02:42.581 --> 00:02:47.503
Some boys were older than Nello, and some were younger.

36
00:02:47.504 --> 00:02:51.448
All of them were with parents or friends.

37
00:02:51.449 --> 00:02:57.865
Nello's heart was sick with fear as he found an empty place on the steps.

38
00:02:57.866 --> 00:03:01.248
He held Patrasche close.

39
00:03:01.249 --> 00:03:07.179
At noon, the great bells of Antwerp's City Hall rang loudly.

40
00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:11.006
The doors at the top of the stairs opened.

41
00:03:11.007 --> 00:03:13.773
The crowd rushed forward.

42
00:03:13.774 --> 00:03:20.228
The winning picture would be displayed high on a wall inside the entrance.

43
00:03:20.229 --> 00:03:24.100
Nello looked up, but he couldn't see.

44
00:03:24.101 --> 00:03:27.079
Too many people were in the way.

45
00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:32.433
Everyone was stretching and pushing to see the winning picture.

46
00:03:32.434 --> 00:03:37.427
At last the crowd thinned and he saw it!

47
00:03:37.428 --> 00:03:40.153
It was not his.

48
00:03:40.154 --> 00:03:43.041
Nello felt dizzy.

49
00:03:43.042 --> 00:03:47.887
With Patrasche's help, he staggered outside.

50
00:03:47.888 --> 00:03:54.949
"It's all over, Patrasche," Nello murmured. "All over."

51
00:03:54.950 --> 00:04:01.386
They both felt weak from lack of food, and walked slowly back to the village.

52
00:04:01.387 --> 00:04:06.661
Snow was starting to fall, and a storm was coming.

53
00:04:06.662 --> 00:04:10.699
It was four o'clock when they reached the village.

54
00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:13.823
Suddenly, Patrasche stopped.

55
00:04:13.824 --> 00:04:17.076
He smelled something in the snow.

56
00:04:17.077 --> 00:04:24.626
He pushed his nose into the snow and picked up a small leather bag with his teeth.

57
00:04:24.627 --> 00:04:27.963
Patrasche gave the bag to Nello.

58
00:04:27.964 --> 00:04:30.879
Nello looked at it closely.

59
00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:35.207
The name on the bag said Master Cogez.

60
00:04:35.208 --> 00:04:44.781
Inside was two thousand francs ─ enough to buy a small farm!

